<title>USA: Exporters sell 100,000 tonnes US corn to unknown.</title>
<headline>Exporters sell 100,000 tonnes US corn to unknown.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private exporters reported the sale of 100,000 tonnes of U.S. corn to unknown buyers for delivery during the 1996/97 marketing year, U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday.</p>
<p>The marketing year ends Aug 30.</p>
<p>By law, exporters must report promptly all sales of 100,000 tonnes or more of a commodity. It sometimes can take a couple of days for the identity of a buyer to become known.</p>
